{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T8N8hjUeshxRMyEV6ZHzut","type":"tool_result","content":"640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n704:- `E.MOVES { a0, a1, z0, z1 }`: a0 / a1 angles (+ = the right side, or up in the screen plane), z0 / z1 heights\n705:- `E.MOVES { reach, r0, r1, hand, plane, blade }`: reach, or r0 / r1 (an extending thrust); hand: 'R' | 'L' | 'both', plane: 'side' (always vertical), blade: 0 (no trail)\n706:- `E.MOVES { wind, active, recover }`: the phases' seconds\n707:- `E.MOVES { kick, spin, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`: the body's motion (kick: true swings the right foot)\n709:- `E.move(name, u = .5, phase = 'active')`: any move from E.MOVES at any moment, for previews and cutscenes: rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) (u 0..1 through phase)\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1152:- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n1153:- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n1154:- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n3:Every public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n28:const E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060225__x4549c1/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"853c3f88-b987-48ff-8d9b-6fb98339dc05","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:06:30.158Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"640:- `new E.Attack(spec = {}, over) → slash`: new E.Attack(spec) or new E.Attack('slash', { reach: 9 }): a name from E.MOVES plus overrides\n703:- `E.MOVES: slash, backslash, overhead, rising, thrust, spin, plunge, twohand, jab, cross, hook, uppercut, haymaker, elbow, ... (24)`: a library of named attacks with timing and body motion (anticipation, lunge, step, twist, hop). new E.Attack('overhead'), new E.Attack('thrust', { reach: 10 }), new E.Combo(['jab', 'cross', 'hook', 'uppercut']) rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) // any move at any moment, for previews and cutscenes The same move works on every build and in every view: heights are relative to the shoulders (rel: true), reaches scale with arm length, and horizontal swings turn into screen-plane swings in side views. A move's spec fields:\n704:- `E.MOVES { a0, a1, z0, z1 }`: a0 / a1 angles (+ = the right side, or up in the screen plane), z0 / z1 heights\n705:- `E.MOVES { reach, r0, r1, hand, plane, blade }`: reach, or r0 / r1 (an extending thrust); hand: 'R' | 'L' | 'both', plane: 'side' (always vertical), blade: 0 (no trail)\n706:- `E.MOVES { wind, active, recover }`: the phases' seconds\n707:- `E.MOVES { kick, spin, lunge, hop, crouch, lean, twist, hold }`: the body's motion (kick: true swings the right foot)\n709:- `E.move(name, u = .5, phase = 'active')`: any move from E.MOVES at any moment, for previews and cutscenes: rig.update(dt, { ..., attack: E.move('roundhouse', .5) }) (u 0..1 through phase)\n91:- 1220 Module arcade: the coin-op's frame: scores, high-score tables and initials, lives, credits, turns, cards, the attract mode (engine/modules/arcade.js); E.Arcade: arcade\n1135:- `new E.Menu(game, items, o = {}) → menu`: Menu with a cursor (title screens, pause menus, shops, battle commands). const menu = new E.Menu(game, ['START', 'OPTIONS', { label: 'CONTINUE', disabled: !save }], { onPick(i, item) {...}, onCancel() {...} }); update: menu.update(dt) draw: menu.draw(r) opts: { x: 'center' | px, y: 'center' | px, title, box: true, color, pick: '#ffd36a', columns: 1 }\n1136:- `menu.draw(r)`: draw it to the overlay\n1137:- `menu.selected`: the entry under the cursor\n1138:- `menu.update()`: move the cursor (up, down; held keys repeat; the mouse over an entry) and pick (confirm, or a click or tap on an entry) or cancel; returns true when it picked or cancelled\n1139:- `menu.active = true`: false stops it reading input\n1140:- `menu.bg = '#141a3a'`, `menu.border = '#e8e4ff'`: the window's colors\n1141:- `menu.box = true`: draw a window round it\n1142:- `menu.color = '#ffffff'`: the entries' color\n1143:- `menu.dim = '#6a6488'`: disabled entries' color\n1144:- `menu.game`: its game\n1145:- `menu.i = 0`: the one under the cursor\n1146:- `menu.input = null` †: the one input it reads (default: every player's, so any player moves and picks; the mouse and taps are player 1's)\n1147:- `menu.items`: the entries (strings, or { label, disabled })\n1148:- `menu.onCancel = null`: called on cancel\n1149:- `menu.onMove = null`: called (i, item) when the cursor moves\n1150:- `menu.onPick = null`: called (i, item) on confirm\n1151:- `menu.pick = '#ffd36a'`: the color of the one under the cursor\n1152:- `menu.sound = true`: false silences it\n1153:- `menu.title = null`: a heading, or null\n1154:- `menu.x = 'center'`, `menu.y = 'center'`: where it sits, 'center' or pixels\n1222:- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n3:Every public name in `engine/my-3d2dge.js` and its modules (`engine/modules/`: a section each, after the core's), one line each: its signature (and default, for a field) and what its doc comment says (a long one's options on lines of their own: `new E.Game({ expand })`). Written by `node tools/api-index.mjs` from the engine itself; `doctrine-check` fails when a public name has no description here. Search it for a name; `API.md` and the agent edition's header are the overviews. † marks a name the agent edition (`my-3d2dge-agent.js`) doesn't have.\n28:const E = My3D2dge, game = new E.Game({ headless: true, res: 'snes' });\n221:- `E.VIEWS: iso, threequarter, topdown, brawler, side, overhead`: the ready-made views: iso (yaw 45, pitch 30), threequarter (pitch 55), topdown (80), brawler (25), side (0) and overhead (90, scale 1: world x/y = screen pixels); new E.Game({ view: 'iso' }) and game.setView('side') take their names\n303:- `input.rebindable(a, map = this.preset)` †: can the player rebind action a? Every action but the menu's (start, pause, confirm, cancel: they are how a player gets back to the menu), and those the game hides with new E.Game({ menu: { controls: { a: false } } })","stderr":"\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060225__x4549c1/work","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T8N8hjUeshxRMyEV6ZHzut","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghwMrhJXaiTsPTso8Efz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Bw23gYAP6GC3xgi1AxoLd1","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /tmp/s55eng/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 1222,1260p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"menu.items\\|opts.menu\\|o.menu\" my-3d2dge.js | head -30; grep -n \"glyphs\" my-3d2dge.js | head -30"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":11549,"cache_read_input_tokens":107544,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":11549},"output_tokens":20,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"9163f3d8-bdc0-4f1f-9f7b-5857347a3a15","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:06:32.719Z","request_id":"req_011CghwMrNi4kNwBCfvYynpu","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01Bw23gYAP6GC3xgi1AxoLd1":{"command":"cd /tmp/s55eng/my-3d2dge/dist/handoff; sed -n 1222,1260p API-INDEX.md | cut -c1-400; grep -n \"menu.items\\|opts.menu\\|o.menu\" my-3d2dge.js | head -30; grep -n \"glyphs\" my-3d2dge.js | head -30"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Bw23gYAP6GC3xgi1AxoLd1","type":"tool_result","content":"- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n- `arcade.add(points, at)`: add points to the player up (at: a world point { x, y, z } where they float up); an extra life at each threshold\n- `arcade.attract(dt)`: the attract mode, each step on the title: 'title', 'demo' (o.idle seconds without input; it lasts o.demo seconds or until endDemo()), 'scores' (o.scores seconds), then 'title' again; any input goes back to 'title'\n- `arcade.card(text, seconds = 2)`: a card in the middle of the screen for seconds ('STAGE 2', 'PLAYER 2, READY!')\n- `arcade.carding`: is a card up? (hold play while it is)\n- `arcade.clear()`: take every card and word down\n- `arcade.coin()`: add a coin (credits on); returns the credits\n- `arcade.continue(seconds = 10, done)`: a continue: CONTINUE? counts down seconds; start, confirm or a tap continues (with the credits it takes): every player's lives back, the scores kept, done(true); at zero, done(false)\n- `arcade.continuing`: is the continue counting down?\n- `arcade.die()`: a life lost: 'again' (lives left), 'next' (the other player's turn) or 'over' (none left for anyone)\n- `arcade.draw(r, box)`: the frame over the game, after its drawing: the HUD (o.hud: 1UP, HI, 2UP in a row) along the top of box [x, y, w, h] (the playfield; the screen when none), the lives along its foot, the cards, DEMO, the continue and the entry\n- `arcade.drawTable(r, mode = '', y = 40, title = 'HIGH SCORES')`: a table as a screen (the attract mode's, or after a game), its title at y: rank, name, score\n- `arcade.endDemo()`: the demo is over (a demo in a scene of its own: call it on the way back): the attract mode shows the scores\n- `arcade.enter(score, mode = '', done)`: open the initials entry for score; done(name) once it is taken and saved\n- `arcade.qualifies(score, mode = '')`: would score make the top ten (never in a demo)?\n- `arcade.say(text, seconds = 1.2)`: a short word under the cards for seconds ('READY!', 'EXTRA LIFE!')\n- `arcade.start(players = 1, o = {})`: begin a game for 1 or 2 players (taking turns), o: { demo: true } for the attract mode's; spends the credits a game takes unless it is free play or a demo. Returns false without them\n- `arcade.table(mode = '')`: the top ten of a mode: [{ name, score }]\n- `arcade.update(dt)`: a step: the cards count down, the entry and the continue read the keys\n- `arcade.wake()`: the attract mode back to the title, its idle clock at zero (as any input does)\n- `arcade.credits`: coins in (null: free play)\n- `arcade.demo = false`: a demo is playing (no table)\n- `arcade.entry = null`: the initials being entered ({ score, mode, name, i }), or null\n- `arcade.game`: the game it serves\n- `arcade.hi = 0`: the high score shown\n- `arcade.id`: the game's name (its tables')\n- `arcade.mode = 'title'`: 'title' | 'play' | 'over'\n- `arcade.o`: the options\n- `arcade.p = null`: the player up\n- `arcade.phase = 'title'`: the attract mode's, 'title' | 'demo' | 'scores'\n- `arcade.players = []`: [{ n, score, lives, save (the game's own: a stage kept while the other plays), next (the score of the next extra life) }]\n- `arcade.wheel = null`: where the letter wheel was last drawn (taps answer to it): { x, y, cw, up, down, ok } in screen pixels: three columns cw wide from x, the up and down bands [y0, y1], the OK button [x, y, w, h]\n\n## Module click: point-and-click adventures: walk areas with holes, depth, hotspots, verbs, an inventory (engine/modules/click.js)\n\n- `new E.Click(game, o = {}) → click` †: new E.Click(game, { rooms, items, rules, hero, ui, story, room, at, on }): see the manual\n- `click.act(verb, target, item = null)` †: do verb on target (a hotspot's id, or an item's: in the inventory), with item (held) or not: the hero walks there first (a hotspot), then the first rule that matches, else the hotspot's own, else a line. Tests and bots call it\n- `click.at(x, y)` †: what is under a room point: an inventory item never; a hotspot (the nearest-drawn), or null\n- `click.busy` †: true while play waits on it: a fade, a line, a talk, a walk\n2379:    this.settings = new Settings(this, (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.settings) || []);\n2527:    this.input.names = (this.o.menu && this.o.menu.controls) || null;\n2528:    if (this.o.corner !== false && (this.o.menu !== false || this.o.fullscreen !== false)) this._corner = makeCorner(this);\n2530:    if (this.o.menu !== false) new Shell(this, { system: true });\n2573:    const showM = !open && (this.o.menu !== false ? (!!(sh && sh._menu()) || main) && (!play || near || touch) : !!I._touchEl);   // (menu: false: the touch START alone)\n3022:   * game.settings: the player's choices, one property each (game.settings.volume), with the game's own (o.menu.settings)\n3126:  btn('Menu', () => { if (game.o.menu !== false) game.menu(); else game.input._tapCode('Act:menu'); }).innerHTML = cornerIcon(CORNER_ICONS.menu);   // (menu: false: the touch START)\n3908:Object.defineProperty(Game.prototype, 'saves', { configurable: true, get() { return this._saves || (this._saves = new Saves(this, this.o.menu && this.o.menu.saves)); } });\n3912:  const g = sh._game; if (!(g.o.menu && g.o.menu.saves)) return;\n9179:    this._sys = !!o.system; this._std = o.standard !== false && game.o.menu !== false;\n9470:    const acts = (name === 'pause' ? [['Resume', () => this.hide()]] : []).concat(v(s.actions) || [], name === 'pause' && this._std && v(this._game.o.menu && this._game.o.menu.items) || []).filter(Boolean);\n9492:    const g = this._game, fs = g.fullscreen, M = g.o.menu || {}, quit = M.quit === false ? null : M.quit || 'title', help = this._o.screens && this._o.screens.help;\n789:    /** glyphs: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' |\n792:    this.glyphs = 'auto'; this.rumbleScale = .6; this.padLost = false;\n895:   *  button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family) */\n904:  /** the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says */\n906:    if (this.glyphs && this.glyphs !== 'auto') return this.glyphs;\n1302: * 6. PIXEL FONT  3x5 glyphs for in-world numbers and labels\n1354:  normal: { glyphs: parseFont(G57), h: 7, desc: 2, gap: 1, space: 3, upper: false },\n1355:  tiny: { glyphs: parseFont(GLYPHS), h: 5, desc: 0, gap: 2, space: 3, upper: true, mono: 3 }\n1369:  _glyph(f, ch) { return f.glyphs[f.upper ? ch.toUpperCase() : ch] || f.glyphs[ch.toUpperCase()] || f.glyphs['?']; },\n1426:   * Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge.\n2999:  glyphs: { group: 'Controller', label: 'Button symbols', type: 'select', value: 'auto', options: [['auto', 'Auto'], ['xbox', 'Xbox'], ['playstation', 'PlayStation'], ['nintendo', 'Nintendo'], ['generic', 'Positions']], apply: (g, v) => { g.input.glyphs = v; } },\nShell cwd was reset to /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060225__x4549c1/work","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"8da0e42d-889b-4c0d-b60d-6478b5e63693","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:06:32.745Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"- `new E.Arcade(game, o = {}) → arcade`: new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [] (the scores that give a life) or every (a life each that many points), credits: null (free play) or the coins a game takes, idle: 20, demo: 30, scores: 6 (the attract mode's seconds), hud: true, colors: [label, number, highlight] })\n- `arcade.add(po