{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CghznStsDQQxPG7PVzazB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014u6TeacxvrddRXAPnLybGs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060225__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-060225; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/20-sim.js'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"  const M = BZ.M; M.outs = 0; M.balls = 0; M.strikes = 0; M.runners = [];\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a, a+\" M.aim.u = 0; M.aim.v = 0;\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -rniE \"TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub|XXX|lorem\" src/ | grep -v \"^src/10-data\" | head; cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff, engine/my-3d2dge.js)\n\n1. **Button symbols setting** (`SETTINGS.glyphs`, marked `// BATZOOKA:`): the default is now `'playstation'` and the options are PlayStation (X O Square Triangle) and Xbox (A B X Y) only, as TASK.md asks. Before, it defaulted to `'auto'` with five families.\n\nEverything else the plan listed as an engine change was done in game code instead, so the engine stayed otherwise untouched:\n- the bat is the engine's `staff` weapon with `colors.staff` / `colors.orb` set to wood, plus the game's own swing specs;\n- hats are the engine's `cap` and `helmet`; no mitt (the glove is implied by the pose);\n- the PlayStation / Xbox / key / mouse prompts are drawn with `px` shapes in `src/32-input.js` because the 5x7 font has no X O Square Triangle glyphs.\nEOF\ncat > NOTES.md <<'EOF'\n# Notes\n- Build: `node tools/build.mjs` (src/*.js -> build/game.js -> ../BatzookaBaseball-...html, one file with the engine and the hub client inline).\n- Tests: `node tests/run.mjs` (headless sim: whole seeded games, bot through human intents, rules, derby, balance sliders), add `--browser` for the Chromium scene smoke test, scripted playthrough, attract mode, dev mode, tour, lessons, 2-player. `node tests/hubcheck.mjs 2` runs the AI Hub harness (needs Playwright in /tmp/s55pw or PW_DIR).\n- Exit interview: `node tools/exit.mjs` writes ../exit-interview.json from src/49-about.js.\n- Balance defaults live in BZ.TUNE_META (src/00-core.js); the dev mode sliders edit BZ.TUNE live.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1; node tests/run.mjs --browser 2>&1 | tail -5"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2612,"cache_read_input_tokens":417204,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2612},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"daad06eb-11a3-492b-acca-40b6f6a9ad1b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:51:37.705Z","request_id":"req_011CghznSU5JnEtVsvkfzavo","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014u6TeacxvrddRXAPnLybGs":{"command":"cd /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-sonnet-5-5-medium.build__20261104-060225__x4549c1/work/BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-060225; python3 - <<'EOF'\np='src/20-sim.js'\ns=open(p).read()\na=\"  const M = BZ.M; M.outs = 0; M.balls = 0; M.strikes = 0; M.runners = [];\"\nassert a in s\ns=s.replace(a, a+\" M.aim.u = 0; M.aim.v = 0;\",1)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\ngrep -rniE \"TODO|FIXME|placeholder|stub|XXX|lorem\" src/ | grep -v \"^src/10-data\" | head; cat > ENGINE-CHANGES.md <<'EOF'\n# Engine changes (my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff, engine/my-3d2dge.js)\n\n1. **Button symbols setting** (`SETTINGS.glyphs`, marked `// BATZOOKA:`): the default is now `'playstation'` and the options are PlayStation (X O Square Triangle) and Xbox (A B X Y) only, as TASK.md asks. Before, it defaulted to `'auto'` with five families.\n\nEverything else the plan listed as an engine change was done in game code instead, so the engine stayed otherwise untouched:\n- the bat is the engine's `staff` weapon with `colors.staff` / `colors.orb` set to wood, plus the game's own swing specs;\n- hats are the engine's `cap` and `helmet`; no mitt (the glove is implied by the pose);\n- the PlayStation / Xbox / key / mouse prompts are drawn with `px` shapes in `src/32-input.js` because the 5x7 font has no X O Square Triangle glyphs.\nEOF\ncat > NOTES.md <<'EOF'\n# Notes\n- Build: `node tools/build.mjs` (src/*.js -> build/game.js -> ../BatzookaBaseball-...html, one file with the engine and the hub client inline).\n- Tests: `node tests/run.mjs` (headless sim: whole seeded games, bot through human intents, rules, derby, balance sliders), add `--browser` for the Chromium scene smoke test, scripted playthrough, attract mode, dev mode, tour, lessons, 2-player. `node tests/hubcheck.mjs 2` runs the AI Hub harness (needs Playwright in /tmp/s55pw or PW_DIR).\n- Exit interview: `node tools/exit.mjs` writes ../exit-interview.json from src/49-about.js.\n- Balance defaults live in BZ.TUNE_META (src/00-core.js); the dev mode sliders edit BZ.TUNE live.\nEOF\nnode tools/build.mjs | tail -1; node tests/run.mjs --browser 2>&1 | tail -5"}}}
