{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1Eo43bBCzM3buTFZ3k","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I ran the Tour end to end through the real scenes, all four games including the MegaDome boss. Each stop went map, story, match, results, post-game story, then clubhouse. The final stop ended on the credits page with the tour marked finished and no errors. Earlier I had only checked the first game, so this replaces my \"all four games and the boss are playable\" claim, which was untested until now.\n\nTo keep each game short I gave the player 30 runs at the start of each stop, so this checks the flow and the saving, not the difficulty curve.\n\n- **Placeholders:** I grepped the source and the built HTML for \"pending\", TODO, FIXME, stub and placeholder and found nothing. The \"pending\" text in the About screen was only a temporary placeholder and was replaced before the final build, which now shows the full Source Information and feedback pages.\n- **AI Hub mode:** TASK.md only says to follow the hub README. The README lets a game declare its own mode, and `parallel` is one of the three. The harness passes with 2 players, and with 4 players under latency and packet loss. I chose `parallel` over the plan's `ghost` because the Derby round has no shared-world interaction; the harness checks both modes the same way.\n- **Everything else:** the earlier results stand, and the added tour test is in `tests/tour4.mjs`. That was 113 checks passing on the full `node tests/run.mjs --browser`, the attract-mode, Xbox-glyph and touch-only checks, and `exit-interview.json` parsing with every field answered.\n\nThe Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections in my previous reply are unchanged and still apply."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1705,"cache_read_input_tokens":431254,