{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1G3ZxAHn1cFHm8wwym","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I loaded the built file in a browser and checked the About pages directly. All six (About, Source Information, Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback, Credits) hold real text, and none contains \"pending\".\n\nThe hub README says \"A game declares one mode\" and lists `parallel`, `ghost` and `shared-world` as equally valid. Nothing in TASK.md names a mode, so `parallel` follows the requirement, and the harness passes with it for 2 players and for 4 under latency and packet loss. I chose it over the plan's `ghost` because the Derby round needs no shared-world interaction.\n\nOn the Tour, my last run played all four stops, including the MegaDome boss, through the real scenes, from map and story to match, results, post-game story and clubhouse. It used a 30-run head start per game, so it proves the flow and the saving, not the difficulty. The full `node tests/run.mjs --browser` passed all 113 checks, with no TODO, FIXME, stub or placeholder strings in the source or the built file.\n\nThe single HTML file is in the work folder root and `exit-interview.json` sits beside it; it parses and every field is answered. Here are the four sections again in full.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:02:25\n- **Source:** baseball (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; TASK.md won where they differed)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (baseball) with a slapstick brawl mini-game (the Rhubarb) and a short story Tour; three-quarter broadcast camera framed behind the plate for the pitch duel with a strike-zone inset, pulling out to follow the ball\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 handoff engine (modified copy, one change), plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified, Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native HD Humanoid pixel-art rigs on generated, textured ballparks in four themed parks (cornfield, moon, volcano, corporate megadome), with lights, weather, fire trails and dust clouds\n- **Animation:** the engine's Humanoid rig and E.MOVES plus custom swing and bunt specs, poses and a Blob mascot; no motion-capture files\n- **Audio:** all in code with the engine's chip synth: six original songs with a tension layer, sound effects, an organ charge call, Animalese-style babble voices; no audio files\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, parallel mode (Derby round); otherwise local play for 1–4 players\n- **Testing:** headless only: seeded whole-game sims, a bot through human intents, a Chromium smoke test and playthrough, a four-stop Tour run, the AI Hub harness; no subagents\n- **Research:** read TASK.md, PLAN.md, the engine card, the sports kit and the hub protocol; nothing else\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in headless Chromium 153)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About nine: a derby soft-lock when a pitcher fielded the ball, more than three outs after a double play, a pitch model that put 40 balls a game outside the zone, exit speeds that made 58 runs a game, wild throws aimed at the base instead of the baseman, a deep link cancelled by the first scene change, a mascot update call that threw, camera framing that hid the batter, and a test harness that forgot to feed the bot its inputs.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the derby soft-lock, the unplayable balance, and the dropped deep link.\n- **Most helpful test:** thirty seeded CPU-versus-CPU games across the four parks with per-game event counts. In seconds it showed that strikeouts never happened and that scores and walks were far off.\n- **Least helpful test:** screenshots of timing-dependent moments. Headless rendering ran at about 12 frames a second, so game state drifted from the wall clock until I stepped the game with `game.advance`.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with E.MOVES, the TileMap `floorTex` hook for painting a ballpark from geometry, headless `game.advance`, and the built-in pause, settings, rebinding and full screen.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes: the three-quarter view is not one pixel per unit, which hid the plate at first; the Backdrop does not show in ground views; `game.after` timers die with a scene change; the staff weapon draws a gem, so my bat looked like a wand until I set the orb color.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the whole baseball: rules, pitch and contact model, ball physics with fence and foul geometry, fielding AI, force and tag logic, baserunning, the Batzooka meter, CPU players and a bot, plus the ballpark generator and the button-glyph renderer.\n- **Hardest part:** keeping a 240-pixel-tall buffer legible with one camera for both the pitch duel and fielding, around the HUD and prompts.\n- **What I changed:** only the Button symbols setting, now PlayStation by default with Xbox as the option.\n- **One change I'd make:** a first-class \"plate cam\" ground view with depth scaling that works with the TileMap, and bat and glove as Humanoid weapon types.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** a real vertical slice with attract mode, dev sliders, hub integration and a one-command headless test, plus the machine-readable exit interview.\n- **Confusing:** the plan is about 150 KB and asks for things that conflict with medium effort (Mode 7 plate cam, motion-capture clips, engine edits); its file names use an older stamp than TASK.md; hub mode was ghost in the plan but it was unclear which mattered.\n- **Hardest thing:** scope. Fielding, running, a CPU, four modes, a tour and a hub round all interact, and each needed a feel pass without a human at the controller.\n- **What I'd change:** add a ranked must-have versus nice-to-have list to the plan, say once which of plan and task wins per conflict, and say how much of the plan is expected at each effort level."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":715,"cache_read_input_tokens":433844,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":715},"output_tokens":739,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"5c83d922-382b-4a1a-93c9-0a1c56d05444","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:57:49.929Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1G3AdmCN7YxcfKKgNm"}
