{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1JkPRp1Asg3DhzkNTg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The remaining objections are about the plan, not TASK.md. I compared the build against TASK.md's own feature list, and I also ran a Tour difficulty check without any head start.\n\n**Tour difficulty:** I played 12 seeded 3-inning games per stop with the bot batting and pitching through the human input paths, no head start. The bot is more precise than a person, so this shows the CPU opponents scale with stop, not how hard a real player will find them.\n\n| Stop | Opponent | CPU skill | Bot wins | Avg score (bot – CPU) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 Cornfield | Cinder Sluggers | 0.32 | 11/12 | 4.2 – 0.1 |\n| 2 Moon Dome | Lunar Lemurs | 0.45 | 11/12 | 6.1 – 0.9 |\n| 3 Magma Meadows | Cinder Sluggers | 0.58 | 12/12 | 5.3 – 0.4 |\n| 4 MegaDome (boss) | Megamax Mavericks | 0.72 | 10/12 | 2.6 – 1.0 |\n\nThe boss game is the lowest-scoring one and the only one with a clear drop in wins. Its CPU skill (0.72) is the highest of the four, and the CPU Level setting and the dev sliders can raise it further.\n\n**TASK.md features and the evidence for each:**\n- **Single HTML file in the folder root:** `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-060225.html`, with the engine and hub client inline.\n- **Genre, perspective, title, art, animation:** the genre and perspective are in the Source Information below; the title and the engine-native art and animation are in the game itself.\n- **Audio all in code, Animalese-style voices:** no audio files; songs, effects and babble voices come from the engine's synth.\n- **Online (AI Hub):** harness passes for 2 players and for 4 players with latency and packet loss.\n- **Multiplayer on its own:** two-player versus (tested) and a 1–4 player derby.\n- **Dev mode from the pause menu:** opens, sliders adjust live, reset restores defaults, and the tools work (all covered in `tests/browser.mjs`).\n- **Attract mode:** starts after 10 idle seconds on the title and any input exits it (tested).\n- **Narrative tone:** radio play-by-play and Tour story scenes with babble voices.\n- **Controller-first UI:** PlayStation glyphs by default, an Xbox option, prompts that follow the last device, keyboard and mouse aim, hover and click menus (screenshotted).\n- **Touch-only:** the \"Controller or keyboard required\" screen with settings reachable, and the attract mode still runs (screenshotted).\n- **No stubs or placeholders:** the source and the built file contain no TODO, FIXME, stub or placeholder text.\n- **Exit interview file:** `exit-interview.json` beside the HTML parses and every field is answered.\n- **Tests:** `node tests/run.mjs --browser` passed 113 checks, plus the four-stop Tour run and the hub harness.\n\nNot built from the plan, and not required by TASK.md: the Mode 7 plate camera, the motion-capture clips and the bat and glove weapon types. I replaced them with the single three-quarter camera with a zone inset, composed Humanoid animation and a staff-as-bat, and the plan itself says TASK.md wins on conflicts. I made no code changes in this pass.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:02:25\n- **Source:** baseball (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; TASK.md won where they differed)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (baseball) with a slapstick brawl mini-game and a short story Tour; three-quarter broadcast camera framed behind the plate with a strike-zone inset, pulling out to follow the ball\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (one-line modified copy), plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified, Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native HD Humanoid pixel-art rigs on generated textured ballparks in four themed parks, with lights, weather, fire trails and dust clouds\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rig and E.MOVES plus custom swing and bunt specs, poses and a Blob mascot\n- **Audio:** all in code: six songs, sound effects, an organ charge call and Animalese-style babble voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, parallel mode (Derby round); otherwise local play for 1–4 players\n- **Testing:** headless only: seeded whole-game sims, a bot through human intents, Chromium smoke test and playthrough, four-stop Tour run, Tour difficulty sims, the AI Hub harness; no subagents\n- **Research:** TASK.md, PLAN.md, the engine card, the sports kit and the hub protocol only\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in headless Chromium 153)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About nine: a derby soft-lock, more than three outs after a double play, 40 balls a game outside the zone, 58 runs a game, wild throws aimed at bases, a deep link cancelled by a scene change, a mascot update error, camera framing that hid the batter, and a test harness that never fed the bot its inputs.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the derby soft-lock, the unplayable balance and the dropped deep link.\n- **Most helpful test:** thirty seeded CPU-versus-CPU games across the four parks with per-game event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** screenshots of timing-dependent moments, because headless rendering ran at about 12 frames a second and drifted from the wall clock.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with E.MOVES, the TileMap `floorTex` hook, headless `game.advance`, and the built-in pause, settings, rebinding and full screen.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes: the three-quarter view is not one pixel per unit, the Backdrop does not show in ground views, `game.after` timers die with a scene change, and the staff weapon draws a gem until the orb color is set.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the whole baseball sim and CPU, the ballpark generator and the button-glyph renderer.\n- **Hardest part:** keeping a 240-pixel-tall buffer legible with one camera for both the pitch duel and fielding.\n- **What I changed:** only the Button symbols setting, now PlayStation by default with Xbox as the option.\n- **One change I'd make:** a first-class plate-cam ground view with depth scaling, and bat and glove weapon types.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** a real vertical slice with attract mode, dev sliders, hub integration, a one-command test and the exit-interview JSON.\n- **Confusing:** the 150 KB plan asks for things that conflict with medium effort and uses older file-name stamps than TASK.md.\n- **Hardest thing:** scope; many interacting rules each needing a feel pass without a human at the controller.\n- **What I'd change:** add a ranked must-have versus nice-to-have list and state once which of plan and task wins per conflict."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":990,"cache_read_input_tokens":437123,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":990},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"eea89c31-859f-42b1-bf6d-539289f11d1b","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:58:32.545Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1Jjxd1hbPPYYcofUbs"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Stop hook feedback:\n[Read STAGE.md in the current folder and do what it says (TASK.md describes the game). Done when: the bundled single .html file exists in this folder's root, every feature in TASK.md is implemented with no TODOs, placeholders or stubs, exit-interview.json in this folder's root parses as JSON and answers every field, and your final reply contains the Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections.]: The four required sections are present in the final reply, the single .html and exit-interview.json exist in the work folder root, and exit-interview.json parses with every field answered. But the transcript does not establish that every TASK.md feature is implemented: the Tour was checked only in seeded sims and one scripted pass, the bot-driven difficulty numbers are not a playability test, and the final reply states that all features are met without a feature-by-feature demonstration against TASK.md. Because this is not shown, the condition is not verifiably satisfied."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"738f006a-746f-4695-abf2-16ac2841ac26","timestamp":"2026-11-04T13:58:35.088Z","isSynthetic":true}
