{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1YN2QXjZ3j1ewjvo5S","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The final full run passed all 113 checks (`node tests/run.mjs --browser`). In this last pass I also confirmed that the HTML and `exit-interview.json` are in the work folder root and that the JSON parses with every field answered.\n\nThe processes the `pgrep` listing showed belong to another agent's run, not mine. I stopped my own hub servers by PID.\n\nA TODO/FIXME/stub/placeholder scan of the source and the built file finds one hit, a comment inside the engine (\"a placeholder in the repo that tools/stamp.mjs replaces\") that is not part of the game.\n\nWhat I can say against TASK.md:\n\n| TASK.md feature | Evidence |\n|---|---|\n| Single HTML file | in the work folder root, 1.4 MB, engine and hub client inline |\n| Dev mode from the pause menu, live sliders, reset | tested in Chromium |\n| Attract mode (starts after 10 idle seconds, any input exits) | tested |\n| Multiplayer on one machine | two-player versus finishes, tested; derby takes 1–4 players |\n| AI Hub | harness passes with 2 players, and 4 players with latency and loss |\n| PlayStation/Xbox prompts, keyboard and mouse, touch-only notice | screenshotted |\n| Narrative tone | radio play-by-play and Tour story scenes with babble voices |\n| No stubs or placeholders | scan above |\n\nMy checks of the Tour were: a four-stop run with a 30-run head start per game, and the bot-driven difficulty simulation. I never played the Tour by hand, so how it feels to a person is untested.\n\nThe Source Information, Testing Feedback, Engine Feedback and Prompt Feedback sections are in my previous reply, and the same text is in the About screen and `exit-interview.json`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1845,"cache_read_input_tokens":443675,"cache_creation":{"