{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgi1ZNf8mJrBkh7fFAwfT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The work is finished, with two limits I can't remove from here. I can't hold a controller or touch a screen, and I can't judge by hand how the Tour feels to a person. The Tour is not a TASK.md feature, since TASK.md only requires a complete demo; it is my own addition from the plan, and my tests played all four stops through the real scenes. No TODOs, stubs or placeholders remain in the game; the only hit in the built file is a comment inside the engine.\n\nThe single HTML file, `BatzookaBaseball-Baseball-claude-sonnet-5-5-medium-20261104-060225.html` (1.4 MB), and `exit-interview.json` are both in the work folder root. The JSON parses and every field is answered.\n\nVerification:\n- **Tests:** the last full `node tests/run.mjs --browser` run passed 113 checks, covering whole games, a scripted playthrough, attract mode, dev mode, lessons, the Tour, the derby and two-player versus.\n- **AI Hub:** the harness passes with 2 players, and with 4 players under latency and loss.\n- **Controller and touch:** I forced the glyph setting and the touch-only screen and looked at screenshots. I tested no real hardware.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-04 06:02:25\n- **Source:** baseball (over the top arcade style)\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md (by claude-opus-5-5 at max effort; TASK.md won where they differed)\n- **Genre and Perspective:** arcade sports (baseball) with a slapstick brawl mini-game (the Rhubarb) and a short story Tour; three-quarter broadcast camera framed behind the plate with a strike-zone inset, pulling out to follow the ball\n- **Tech:** my-3D2dge v0.85.2 (one-line modified copy), plain JavaScript in one IIFE, AI Hub client 1.4.0 unmodified, Playwright 1.63.0 for tests\n- **Art Direction:** engine-native HD Humanoid pixel-art rigs on generated textured ballparks in four themed parks (cornfield, moon, volcano, megadome), with lights, weather, fire trails and dust clouds\n- **Animation:** engine Humanoid rig and E.MOVES plus custom swing and bunt specs, poses and a Blob mascot\n- **Audio:** all in code: six songs, sound effects, an organ charge call and Animalese-style babble voices\n- **Online:** AI Hub session protocol v1, parallel mode (Derby round); otherwise local play for 1–4 players\n- **Testing:** headless only: seeded whole-game sims, a bot through human intents, Chromium smoke test and playthrough, a four-stop Tour run, the AI Hub harness; no subagents\n- **Research:** TASK.md, PLAN.md, the engine card, the sports kit and the hub protocol only\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux; browser unknown (tested in headless Chromium 153)\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-sonnet-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** unknown\n\n## Testing Feedback\n- **How many issues did testing catch?** About nine: a derby soft-lock, more than three outs after a double play, 40 balls a game outside the zone, 58 runs a game, wild throws aimed at bases, a deep link cancelled by a scene change, a mascot update error, camera framing that hid the batter, and a test harness that never fed the bot its inputs.\n- **How many were critical?** Three: the derby soft-lock, the unplayable balance and the dropped deep link.\n- **Most helpful test:** thirty seeded CPU-versus-CPU games across the four parks with per-game event counts.\n- **Least helpful test:** screenshots of timing-dependent moments, because headless rendering ran at about 12 frames a second and drifted from the wall clock.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n- **Liked most:** Humanoid rigs with E.MOVES, the TileMap `floorTex` hook, headless `game.advance`, and the built-in pause, settings, rebinding and full screen.\n- **Stuck or guessed wrong?** Yes: the three-quarter view is not one pixel per unit, the Backdrop does not show in ground views, `game.after` timers die with a scene change, and the staff weapon draws a gem until the orb color is set.\n- **Most important thing built myself:** the whole baseball sim and CPU, the ballpark generator and the button-glyph renderer.\n- **Hardest part:** keeping a 240-pixel-tall buffer legible with one camera for both the pitch duel and fielding.\n- **What I changed:** only the Button symbols setting, now PlayStation by default with Xbox as the option.\n- **One change I'd make:** a first-class plate-cam ground view with depth scaling, and bat and glove weapon types.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n- **Liked most:** a real vertical slice with attract mode, dev sliders, hub integration, a one-command test and the exit-interview JSON.\n- **Confusing:** the 150 KB plan asks for things that conflict with medium effort and uses older file-name stamps than TASK.md.\n- **Hardest thing:** scope; many interacting rules each needing a feel pass without a human at the controller.\n- **What I'd change:** add a ranked must-have versus nice-to-have list and state once which of plan and task wins per conflict."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":909,"cache_read_input_tokens":445520,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":909},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ae684082-f21f-4a2b-8baf-c73d93056a9d","uuid":"bd8fd3a9-82a4-43af-b169-8e9c5c9878f1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T14:01:43.877Z","request_id":"req_011Cgi1ZNFaZSVxCto9TWgps"}
